      "answer": "The arrow anti-pattern occurs when code has many levels of nested if statements, creating a shape that looks like a sideways arrow (>>>>).\n\nArrow anti-pattern:\nif (condition1) {\n    if (condition2) {\n        if (condition3) {\n            if (condition4) {\n                doSomething();\n            }\n        }\n    }\n}\n\nWays to avoid:\n1. Use guard clauses:\nif (!condition1) return;\nif (!condition2) return;\nif (!condition3) return;\ndoSomething();\n\n2. Combine conditions:\nif (condition1 && condition2 && condition3) {\n    doSomething();\n}\n\n3. Extract methods:\nif (allConditionsMet()) {\n    doSomething();\n}"
