        "question": "Write a program using nested if to implement a university admission system with stream allocation.",
        "solution": "import java.util.Scanner;\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);\n        System.out.print(\"Enter total marks (out of 400): \");\n        int total = sc.nextInt();\n        System.out.print(\"Enter Math marks: \");\n        int math = sc.nextInt();\n        System.out.print(\"Enter Science marks: \");\n        int science = sc.nextInt();\n        if (total >= 240) {\n            System.out.println(\"Eligible for admission.\");\n            if (math >= 80 && science >= 75) {\n                System.out.println(\"Stream: SCIENCE\");\n                if (math >= 95) {\n                    System.out.println(\"Branch: Computer Science\");\n                } else if (science >= 85) {\n                    System.out.println(\"Branch: Electronics\");\n                } else {\n                    System.out.println(\"Branch: Mechanical\");\n                }\n            } else if (math >= 70) {\n                System.out.println(\"Stream: COMMERCE\");\n            } else {\n                System.out.println(\"Stream: ARTS\");\n            }\n        } else {\n            System.out.println(\"Not eligible. Need \" + (240 - total) + \" more marks.\");\n        }\n        sc.close();\n    }\n}",
        "output": "Enter total marks (out of 400): 320\\nEnter Math marks: 92\\nEnter Science marks: 85\\nEligible for admission.\\nStream: SCIENCE\\nBranch: Computer Science"
